### CampusEats API Testing - Orders & Kitchen Features

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5168

### ===============================
### MENU ENDPOINTS (for reference)
### ===============================

### Create Menu Item - Burger
POST {{baseUrl}}/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Burger",
  "price": 8.99
}

### Create Menu Item - Pizza
POST {{baseUrl}}/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pizza",
  "price": 12.50
}

### Create Menu Item - Salad
POST {{baseUrl}}/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Salad",
  "price": 6.99
}

### Get All Menu Items
GET {{baseUrl}}/menu

### ===============================
### ORDER ENDPOINTS (Week 3)
### ===============================

### Create Order
# Note: Replace menuItemId values with actual IDs from menu items created above
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user123",
  "items": [
    {
      "menuItemId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "quantity": 2,
      "specialInstructions": "No onions please"
    },
    {
      "menuItemId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "quantity": 1,
      "specialInstructions": "Extra cheese"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Deliver to Room 301"
}

### Get All Orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders

### Get Orders by User ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?userId=user123

### Get Order by ID
# Note: Replace with actual order ID from create order response
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Cancel Order
# Note: Replace with actual order ID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/cancel

### ===============================
### KITCHEN ENDPOINTS (Week 3)
### ===============================

### Get Pending Orders (for kitchen view)
GET {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders

### Update Order Status to Preparing
# Note: Replace with actual order ID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Preparing"
}

### Update Order Status to Ready
# Note: Replace with actual order ID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Ready"
}

### Update Order Status to Completed
# Note: Replace with actual order ID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Completed"
}

### ===============================
### ERROR CASES - Testing Validation
### ===============================

### Invalid Order - Empty Items
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user123",
  "items": [],
  "notes": "This should fail"
}

### Invalid Order - Missing UserId
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "",
  "items": [
    {
      "menuItemId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

### Invalid Order - Quantity <= 0
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user123",
  "items": [
    {
      "menuItemId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "quantity": 0
    }
  ]
}

### Invalid Status Transition
# Try to update a Completed order (should fail)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Preparing"
}

### Invalid Status Value
PUT {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "InvalidStatus"
}

### ===============================
### WORKFLOW TEST SCENARIO
### ===============================

### Step 1: Create menu items
# (Use the menu endpoints above first)

### Step 2: Customer creates an order
# POST {{baseUrl}}/orders

### Step 3: Kitchen views pending orders
# GET {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders

### Step 4: Kitchen starts preparing
# PUT {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders/{id}/status - status: "Preparing"

### Step 5: Kitchen marks as ready
# PUT {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders/{id}/status - status: "Ready"

### Step 6: Customer picks up (marks completed)
# PUT {{baseUrl}}/kitchen/orders/{id}/status - status: "Completed"

### Alternative Step: Customer cancels before preparing
# PUT {{baseUrl}}/orders/{id}/cancel
